# component: table
# decisions: API-16, DOC-1, DOC-2
# hunks:
#   NO STYLING HUNK. Every row this component could have argued with resolves as **shadcn** and
#     therefore ships verbatim: LAY-6 (cells stay `whitespace-nowrap`, the head stays `h-10`
#     `font-medium text-foreground` with no `--table-cell-min-width` wrap), COL-6 (the row hover is
#     upstream's own `hover:bg-muted/50`) and COL-8 (a selected row is `data-[state=selected]:bg-muted`,
#     not a pressed rung). The container is upstream's `data-slot="table-container"` div.
#   API-16: `"use client"` is removed. Every part in this file is a plain element with a class —
#     no hook, no event handler, no browser API, no engine — so the directive marks a wholly
#     presentational module as a client boundary and drags a `<table>` out of the server tree for
#     nothing. API-16 puts the boundary at the LOWEST interactive leaf, and there is no leaf here.
#     `design-lint`'s `presentational-client-boundary` rule reports it, which is how it was found.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
